WebDAV Manga for KOReader - version 0.4.11

Local repair build 2026-10-01 preserves repeated EPUB spine images with
independent page identifiers, refreshes connection-key-owned legacy PDF
opening caches, and opens RAR/CBR after three validated pages using bounded
512 KiB opening reads. Archive order remains stable during background indexing.
On KindleHF only, 7Z/CB7 may use the pinned official LZMA-capable libarchive
in lib/kindlehf when the installed core library lacks that codec. Its source
provenance and complete license notices are included alongside the binary.
No KOReader core library is replaced. Actual server/device acceptance remains
required; solid archives may need prefix decoding for later pages.

Version 0.4.11 opens its supported image-only EPUB, bounded image-PDF, and
device-supported seekable 7Z/CB7 paths after three validated opening pages (or
all pages of a shorter book). Pages 4 through 20 are prioritized after Reader entry,
then the full catalog continues in the background. Jump navigation stays
disabled until that catalog is complete. Complete-source download still needs
explicit confirmation. A failed background catalog keeps readable pages and
offers retry streaming, explicit complete download, or return. This is not universal PDF or 7Z support:
ambiguous,
encrypted, damaged, complex, or device-codec-incompatible inputs remain
unsupported and must report their bounded failure reason.

Version 0.4.10 opens supported remote archives from a bounded twenty-page
index. A single background scan publishes an atomic index snapshot after each
additional five pages, so the active reader can continue before the complete
directory is available. Archives with at most twenty image pages are marked
complete during startup. Page bodies remain on the existing Range and bounded
cache path; this index change does not download the whole source document.

Version 0.4.09 opens supported EPUB, RAR/CBR and 7z/CB7 archives after a
bounded first-five-page index, then completes the shared page index in the
background without downloading the whole source file. It also restores the
single-image PDF compatibility path and accepts libarchive ARCHIVE_WARN when
the current header remains usable. Full-download fallback remains explicit.

Version 0.4.08 restores the 0.3.89-compatible image-PDF and EPUB Range paths,
preserves explicit complete-download confirmation, and reports the failing
stream stage. 7z improvements and the first-five-page progressive index remain
scheduled for 0.4.09. Kindle runtime behavior has not been validated for this
release; desktop tests do not establish device TLS, Range, or performance.

Version 0.4.07 preserves Suwayomi's non-secret OPDS page-mode boolean while
keeping credentials and arbitrary query values redacted. It also raises the
bounded PDF page-index IPC payload to the existing archive manifest limit, so
large remote PDF indexes do not incorrectly fall back to a complete download.

Version 0.4.06 connects the existing premium-license client to its independent
production HTTPS endpoint and verifies receipts with the bundled RSA public key.
No private key, no plaintext activation key, no license database, and no Worker
secret is included in the plugin package. Local authorization remains in the
KOReader settings directory and is not removed by a plugin-folder replacement.
No plaintext activation key is included in any release member.

Version 0.4.05 uses Maximum (GPL-3.0) and Meguru (AGPL-3.0) as behavior
references for quadrant interaction, bounded margin analysis and OPDS pointer
workflows. The behavior was independently implemented in this plugin's existing
Reader, Loader and Library modules. No GPL or AGPL source code was copied.
No upstream Reader, database, updater or server-management code is included.
The named upstream projects retain their own licenses; behavioral reference
does not claim ownership of their code or replace their license notices.

This is an unofficial third-party plugin. It uses KOReader's public plugin,
widget, networking, and storage interfaces and follows standard WebDAV
PROPFIND/GET behavior. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or maintained by
the KOReader project or 极空间.

The implementation was informed by public KOReader APIs and publicly available
WebDAV plugin behavior. It does not copy business logic from the referenced
fanqie.koplugin or weread.koplugin projects. Custom cover rows are implemented
for remote WebDAV resources; they are not copied from KOReader CoverBrowser
business logic. 自定义封面行面向远程 WebDAV 资源实现，不复制 KOReader
CoverBrowser 的业务逻辑。

Swipe_Animation.koplugin was reviewed as a behavioral reference during early
development. Version 0.3.5 does not copy or run its transition code: page
animation is delegated to KOReader's existing Kindle display-driver API and
does not patch KOReader core files.

The plugin only changes its local settings, history, cache, and category index.
It never deletes remote WebDAV files. 插件绝不删除远程 WebDAV 文件。

Version 0.3.41 is rebuilt from the 0.3.21 release and does not include smart
ambient-light sensing or automatic brightness control. Manual frontlight and
color-temperature controls remain available through KOReader's device API.

Version 0.3.41 includes native-document classification and handoff for common
formats, plus validated HTTP Range loading for image pages. Invalid or
unsupported Range responses fall back to a complete GET. WebDAV documents are
staged completely before they are handed to KOReader's native reader.

Version 0.3.64 can index unencrypted image-based MOBI files after the complete
document is local, then copy individual image records into the plugin page
cache on demand. Text-oriented and unrecognized MOBI files remain handled by
KOReader's native document reader.

Version 0.3.70 indexes a fixed-layout remote image-based MOBI from its PalmDB
record table and validates only the first image before opening. Later image
records are downloaded and identified on demand through bounded HTTP Range
reads. Local MOBI parsing and the complete-document fallback remain unchanged.

Version 0.3.71 drains readable subprocess output before waiting for process
exit, preventing large MOBI page indexes from filling the IPC pipe and
deadlocking the opening dialog. Image-oriented legacy MOBI files without an
explicit fixed-layout marker may use the same first-image Range path when the
existing record-count and resource-volume checks identify them as image books.

Version 0.3.72 also uses bounded first-image inspection when a completed MOBI
document cache is opened, so a cache hit does not rescan every image record
before entering the manga reader. Later pages remain extracted on demand and
are probed for their actual image format and dimensions before publication.

Version 0.3.74 streams image pages from remote CBZ archives and image-based
EPUB files through validated HTTP Range reads. Unsupported, protected, and
non-image EPUB files retain the complete-download native-reader fallback.

Version 0.3.73 accepts equal consecutive PalmDB record offsets as zero-length
records while continuing to reject descending and out-of-bounds offsets. This
keeps valid image MOBI files on the bounded HTTP Range path instead of forcing
a complete-document fallback.

Version 0.3.96 adds the local premium-license client skeleton for the isolated
product webdavmanga-premium. Production activation endpoint, RSA public key,
and device RSA verification provider are not configured in this release.
Missing configuration fails closed. Production online activation and Kindle
offline verification remain unverified. Worker source, D1 imports, plaintext
keys and signing private keys are excluded from the plugin distribution.
Authorization does not grant a source-code distribution license.

Version 0.3.33 adds bounded LRU browsing-cache maintenance and a low-cost LUT
image filter. It also preserves validated images whose WebDAV filename
extension differs from the detected image signature. It does not include the
postponed commercial authorization system,
online activation, fixed license keys, device binding, or seven-day trial.

